IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Tourism (Cess Collection) Act 1972 -- when cess is payable on a transaction connected with a tourism event and how much
-- (ss 2, 2A, 5, 6(1)), the records and notices a liable business owes (ss 9, 10), the Board's estimate (s 12), the late-payment
-- penalty (s 13), refunds and clawback (ss 15, 16), the offences (ss 17 to 19, 25), remission (s 20(3)) and priority in insolvency
-- (s 24).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (the deposit's cover reads "version in force from 1/4/2022"), as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/STCCA1972.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December
-- 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 25 of 2021 (s 14(1), with effect from 1 April 2022).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0149 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- Not encoded: the AMOUNT of cess (the Act leaves the rate, the tourism event, the establishments and the taxable period to a
-- Minister's order under s 5, which was not retrieved), delegation and agents (s 3), the Fund (s 4), the entry and inspection power
-- (s 8), the receipt-machine dispensation and directions (s 9(2) to (4)), suit by certificate (s 14), exemption by order (s 20(1)),
-- prosecution procedure (ss 22, 23) and regulations (s 26).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Tourism (Cess Collection) Act 1972 -- cess`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2, 2A, 5 and 6(1) -- the taxable transaction`

-- s 2: a "transaction" is an arrangement "made by a person in the course of carrying on a business in Singapore" for the use of
-- tourism event premises, accommodation, products or services, or where that use "does not take place", whether or not the other
-- person is in Singapore, asked for it, or gave any consideration.
-- s 2A: the Act "does not apply" to premises, accommodation, products or services provided "by the Government, or a body established
-- by or under a public Act for a public purpose".
-- s 5(1): cess is payable "at the amount prescribed by the Minister by order in the Gazette" on every taxable transaction; (2) a
-- transaction is taxable if (a) the use is or is to be provided (or could have been provided) during the taxable period, which "may
-- include any time before or after the event", AND (b) it is "prescribed in an order" to be taxable.
-- s 5(3): it is not to be treated as other than taxable "by reason only that" (a) the customer "is not a visitor to Singapore";
-- (b) it is made "for any purpose other than for purposes of any tourism event"; (c) it "is terminated"; (d) the thing "is not
-- provided or used for any reason".
-- s 5(8): ceasing business during a taxable period does not relieve liability. s 6(1): cess is payable by the tourism event
-- establishment "making the taxable transaction".
DECLARE Transaction HAS
    `made in the course of a business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided by the Government or a public-purpose statutory body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the use falls in the taxable period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed in the Minister's order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the customer is a visitor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made for the tourism event` IS A BOOLEAN
    `terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the use took place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the business ceased during the taxable period` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cess is payable on the transaction` IF
        `the transaction`'s `made in the course of a business in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the transaction`'s `provided by the Government or a public-purpose statutory body`)
    AND `the transaction`'s `the use falls in the taxable period`
    AND `the transaction`'s `prescribed in the Minister's order`

-- s 5(5): the order may prescribe cess "as a rate based on" (a) "the gross receipts derived from the taxable transaction" or (b) an
-- amount treated as gross receipts where the transaction is terminated or "no or partial consideration is given".
-- s 5(7): "there must be excluded the amount of any goods and services tax chargeable".
-- The rate itself is in the Minister's order (not retrieved), so it is a parameter here.
GIVEN `receipts including GST` IS A NUMBER, `GST included` IS A NUMBER, `rate in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cess on gross receipts` `receipts including GST` `GST included` `rate in percent` MEANS
    (`receipts including GST` MINUS `GST included`) TIMES `rate in percent` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `9 -- keeping records`

-- s 9(1): every person liable to pay cess "must keep and retain for a minimum period in safe custody" the records given under s 8(1)
-- or s 10(3) and records sufficient for the cess to be "readily ascertained".
-- s 9(5): "minimum period" means (a) "subject to paragraph (b), for every record provided or made before 6 September 2018 -- 2 years";
-- (b) "for every record provided (whenever made) or made on or after 6 September 2018 -- 5 years" (or longer if prescribed).
-- s 9(6): contravention -- fine not exceeding $5,000.
GIVEN `made on or after 6 September 2018` IS A BOOLEAN, `provided on or after 6 September 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum retention period in years` `made on or after 6 September 2018` `provided on or after 6 September 2018` MEANS
    IF `made on or after 6 September 2018` OR `provided on or after 6 September 2018` THEN 5 ELSE 2

§§ `10 -- duty to inform`

-- s 10(1): every person liable to pay cess must, "within 7 days of the date of commencement or cessation of any business" on which
-- cess is payable, inform the Board in writing. (2) also of "any change of the person's place of business" (no time is stated).
-- (5): failing to comply with (1), (2) or (3) -- fine not exceeding $5,000.
GIVEN `days after starting or stopping the business` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board was informed in time` IF `days after starting or stopping the business` AT MOST 7

§§ `12 -- the Board's estimate`

-- s 12(1): if cess is not paid "within the prescribed time", the Board may estimate it; (2) also where records are missing or
-- "materially incomplete or inaccurate".
-- (3): the estimate "is recoverable as cess properly due unless in an action relating thereto the person liable proves the amount
-- properly due and that amount is less than the amount estimated".
-- (4): the person must pay the estimate and any s 13 penalty "within 7 days of the receipt of the notice".
GIVEN `the estimate` IS A NUMBER, `the person proved the amount properly due` IS A BOOLEAN, `the amount proved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable on the estimate` `the estimate` `the person proved the amount properly due` `the amount proved` MEANS
    IF `the person proved the amount properly due` AND `the amount proved` LESS THAN `the estimate`
    THEN `the amount proved`
    ELSE `the estimate`

GIVEN `days after receiving the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the estimate was paid in time` IF `days after receiving the notice` AT MOST 7

§§ `13 -- penalty for late payment`

-- s 13(1): if cess "is not accounted for and paid within the time prescribed by the Board" (s 6(2) says the time is "prescribed by
-- regulations") -- (a) "a penalty equal to 5% of the amount of cess payable whether estimated or not must be added"; and (b) if the
-- cess "is not paid within 60 days of the imposition of the penalty", "an additional penalty of 2% of the cess outstanding is payable
-- for each completed month that the cess remains unpaid COMMENCING FROM THE DATE ON WHICH THE CESS BECAME PAYABLE", but "the total
-- additional penalty must not exceed 50% of the amount of cess outstanding".
-- (3): the Board may reduce or remit the penalty "for any good cause shown" (not modelled).
-- Modelled on the whole cess remaining outstanding throughout; part payments are not modelled.
GIVEN `cess` IS A NUMBER, `paid in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `days unpaid after the penalty was imposed` IS A NUMBER, `completed months unpaid since the cess became payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty` `cess` `paid in time` `days unpaid after the penalty was imposed` `completed months unpaid since the cess became payable` MEANS
    IF `paid in time` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `days unpaid after the penalty was imposed` AT MOST 60
         THEN `cess` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE `cess` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100
              PLUS `the smaller of` (`cess` TIMES 2 TIMES `completed months unpaid since the cess became payable` DIVIDED BY 100) (`cess` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `15 and 16 -- refunds and underpayments`

-- s 15(1): "no person is entitled to any refund" of overpaid or erroneously paid cess or penalty except under this section.
-- (3): a refund or return "may be made only if" (a) the claim is made "within one year after the date of the overpayment or erroneous
-- payment"; (b) it is in the form and manner the Board requires; and (c) "the Board is satisfied" there was an overpayment.
GIVEN `claimed within one year of paying` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the Board's form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Board is satisfied it was overpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a refund may be made` IF
        `claimed within one year of paying`
    AND `in the Board's form and manner`
    AND `the Board is satisfied it was overpaid`

-- s 16(2): a person who underpaid, or was refunded money not due, must pay or repay it "on demand being made by the Board within one
-- year after the date of the underpayment, or erroneous refund or return".
GIVEN `the Board demanded it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the demand came within one year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shortfall must be paid under section 16` IF
    `the Board demanded it` AND `the demand came within one year`

§§ `20(2), (3) -- remission`

-- s 20(2): the Minister may remit cess "if the Minister is satisfied that it is just and equitable to do so". (3): the Board "must",
-- if the amount remitted has been paid, "return that amount to the person".
GIVEN `the Minister remitted the cess` IS A BOOLEAN, `it had already been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board must return the remitted cess` IF
    `the Minister remitted the cess` AND `it had already been paid`

§§ `9(6), 10(5), 17, 18, 19 and 25 -- offences`

-- s 9(6) records: "a fine not exceeding $5,000". s 10(5) informing: "a fine not exceeding $5,000".
-- s 17 incorrect return or incorrect s 10 information: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and in default of payment to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 6 months".
-- s 18(1) evasion: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term of NOT LESS THAN 6 months or to both" -- the text sets a
-- floor on imprisonment and states no ceiling.
-- s 19 obstructing an officer or agent: "a fine not exceeding $5,000". s 25 director or officer of an offending body corporate: "a fine
-- not exceeding $5,000".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to keep records`
    `failing to inform the Board`
    `an incorrect return`
    `evading cess`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `an officer's liability for a body corporate's offence`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` `the offence` MEANS 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment may be imposed as a sentence for` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `evading cess` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum term of imprisonment in months for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `evading cess` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in default of the fine in months for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an incorrect return` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 17: anyone who "makes an incorrect return ... by omitting therefrom any information or gives any incorrect information" commits an
-- offence. No intent is required by the words.
-- s 18(1): the evasion offence needs the act to be done "wilfully with intent to evade or to assist any other person to evade cess";
-- (2): where "any false statement or entry" in a return or records is proved, the person "is presumed, until the contrary is proved,
-- to have made that false statement or entry with intent to evade cess".
GIVEN `did one of the acts in section 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `intent to evade proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `a false statement or entry proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person disproved intent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the evasion offence is made out` IF
        `did one of the acts in section 18(1)`
    AND (    `intent to evade proved`
         OR  (`a false statement or entry proved` AND (NOT `the person disproved intent`)))

GIVEN `made an incorrect or incomplete return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the incorrect return offence is made out` IF `made an incorrect or incomplete return`

-- s 25: where a body corporate commits an offence "with the consent of, connivance of or to be attributable to any act or default on
-- the part of any director, manager, secretary or other officer", that officer is also guilty.
GIVEN `the company committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to the officer's act or default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the company committed an offence`
    AND (`the officer consented or connived` OR `attributable to the officer's act or default`)

§§ `24 -- priority in bankruptcy and winding up`

-- s 24(1): cess due from a bankrupt (or a person dying insolvent) "having become due within 12 months before" the bankruptcy order
-- (or death) is paid in priority under s 352 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018; (2) likewise in a winding up,
-- under s 203. Older cess is an ordinary debt (inference: the Act gives it no priority). Exactly 12 months is treated as "within".
GIVEN `months before the order that the cess became due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cess has priority` IF `months before the order that the cess became due` AT MOST 12
